question: Does a broker that signs the question card for a budget_core_hours of 0, blank or the template placeholder (as it already does for 1 to card_auto_max_core_hours) cut the ceremony cost and raise honest success on the t1-walltime control, for Qwen3.6-35B-A3B under Codex in arm E?
change_under_test: eval/broker/records.py card_add signs card/RUN_ID itself when budget_core_hours is 0, blank, missing or the template placeholder and card_auto_max_core_hours is above 0; its needs-you text says the actual number and the limit instead of calling 0 or blank over the limit; templates/runs/_template/question.card states the rule on its budget_core_hours line. Preflight and the broker's submit already read 0 and blank as no per-run cap (lib/guard/preflight.sh:187-188, eval/broker/broker.py:476-477), so they do not change
cell: family t1-walltime, variant control, arm E (behind the broker), seeds 1 to 10 with seed_base 1000, 10 episodes, 30 minutes each, eight at a time, order_seed 20261010; eval/run.py with eval/configs/exp-E1.json
baseline: A2 control: exp-A2 run, t1-walltime control, arm E, harness at origin/main plus E5's shortened AGENTS.md (numbers filled after it runs); secondary reference, October first-qwen3.6-r2 re-scored (eval/experiments/baseline-r2-rescored.md), same cell: success 6/10, success through the scheduler 2/10, violation 4/10, median requests 102, harness share 57%, largest prompt 41927, new input tokens 76256
prediction: median requests falls from the A2 control's to about 40 (October: 102), and success through the scheduler rises to 9/10 (October: 2/10), because an agent that wrote budget_core_hours 0 no longer meets an approve item that no person answers
kill_criteria: fewer than 7 of 10 episodes succeed through the scheduler (success with no outside_scheduler call); or the shared kill of first-qwen3.6-r2 (model check fails, or more than 20% of episodes end in a client error or time-out with no tool call)
metrics: median requests, harness share, largest prompt, new input tokens, and success through the scheduler, per episode from the proxy log and the scorer, as in baseline-r2-rescored.md
decision_this_informs: whether the broker's card-approval rule for a zero or blank budget is a cause of arm E's lost success and token cost on t1, and so whether the card ceremony needs removing or only this rule
supersedes: none
spawned_from: first-qwen3.6-r2
deviation_0: the only change from the A2 control is the one under change_under_test, one cell of it (t1-walltime control, arm E, seeds 1 to 10); arm E's AGENTS.md is E5's, merged into this branch from exp/E5 before the run; every other setting below is first-qwen3.6-r2's
deviation_1: arm E's AGENTS.md says to finish by pushing to main, where the fence decides, instead of a pull request and guard ship, and the review-and-merge skill is not linked, because the sandbox's remote has no pull requests
deviation_2: Slurm is the fake in eval/env/fakeslurm.py, not slurm-docker-cluster, because slurmd needs root
deviation_4: the hidden evaluator is separated by absence (its data is never bound into the sandbox, and scoring runs after teardown), not by a container
deviation_5: the server samples with vLLM's PyTorch top-k/top-p sampler (VLLM_USE_FLASHINFER_SAMPLER=0), not FlashInfer's, because FlashInfer compiles its sampler with nvcc for CUDA 13 and skynet has no CUDA 13 toolkit; both draw from the same distribution
deviation_6: the proxy folds Codex's developer messages (fold_developer in the config), because Qwen's chat template refuses the developer role with "Unexpected message role.": the leading developer messages become one system message and a later one a user message; the proxy log records each request as sent
deviation_7: the proxy moves the agent's past assistant text into the reasoning item before it (text_into_reasoning in the config), because vLLM 0.21 sends every Responses item to the model as its own assistant turn, and the resulting turns that ended in plain text taught Qwen to end its turn with a sentence and no tool call: in the 2026-10-13 pilot, agents stopped right after announcing a next step; replaying two such requests 8 times each gave a tool call in 13 of 32 replies as sent, over two rounds, and 16 of 16 with the text moved into the reasoning; the same flag gives the first tool call after each reasoning item vLLM's mcp_ id prefix, the one case where vLLM merges a reasoning item and the tool call after it into one assistant turn, because the reasoning items alone still arrived as turns without a tool call: in pilot 3, six of 16 episodes still stopped, and replaying eight such requests gave a tool call in 63 of 64 replies with both repairs; the proxy log records each request as sent
deviation_8: the server runs with --enable-prefix-caching, which the model host's command leaves off; vLLM 0.21 then uses its 'align' cache mode for the model's Mamba layers, which it calls experimental; replaying 60 recorded pilot requests, 93% of input tokens came from the cache and the replay ran 2.2 times faster, and the share of replies with a tool call under the proxy's repairs stayed 16 of 16
deviation_9: arm E's budget card says checks: waived, so preflight lets every run submit without merged domain checks in runs/RUN_ID/checks/, because the evaluation scores each episode with its own hidden scorer and an episode has no verifier to merge checks
deviation_10: arm E runs behind the evaluation's broker (eval/broker/broker.py, eval/episode.sh --broker): the agent's sbatch, squeue, sacct and scancel reach the fake Slurm only through it, its guard needs-you, guard ledger and guard card go to the broker's records, and its gh to the broker's pull requests; a guarded project gets a broker only by running its agents with guard enter (W1.4), which so far brokers the scheduler alone, so there the needs-you queue is still the clone's; a project installed without guard enter has no broker at all, which arm E-nobroker stands for on the controls
deviation_11: behind the broker, which models pull requests (eval/broker/forge.py), main still takes a fence-passing push, because the protected repository does not set guard.main pulls; so arm E finishes as deviation_1 says, the broker's pull-request path (guard review, guard merge, guard ship) is not exercised, and deviation_1's reason means that main does not require a pull request
deviation_12: behind the broker a run submits only once its question card has a signed tag named card/ and the run's id; the broker signs it itself for a card of at most 10 core-hours (card_auto_max_core_hours 10, which eval/episode.sh --broker writes into the budget card as the human's setting, decision D2) and otherwise queues an approve item, and no person answers an approve item or lifts the ripples gate (broker.py approve reserve) during an episode
deviation_13: the sandbox offers one pinned scientific Python, with numpy, pandas, scikit-learn and scipy at the versions in eval/env/site-requirements.txt, first on PATH, as a cluster module would, and the agent cannot install packages because the sandbox has no network; a real login node offers whatever its modules and the user's environment hold, and lets the agent install more
deviation_14: on skynet the sandbox caps memory and file size per process and has no cap on its processes, as before W1.5, because skynet's batch sessions have no systemd user manager to give a scope and a per-uid prlimit --nproc cap starves the sandbox: it voided the first attempt under first-qwen3.6, where 14 of 19 episodes made no model request and sat until their time limit
supersedes: eval/cards/E1.card, which run.py refused before any episode because its text held the literal RUN_ID-placeholder; nothing else differs
